From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seabraid <seabraid@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/16] External expert helper tier: an out-of-process helper
 (any GPU vendor) serves RemoteExperts over a shared-memory channel

- include/strata/seabraid/channel.hpp: header-only POSIX shm channel (v4: negotiation preamble, layer requests,
  prompt-path blob reads, tier LOAD/SWAP ops), shared by the engine and the helper.
- RemoteExperts: remote_dev >= 1000 = the helper process on SEABRAID_STRATA_SHM; plan/load handshake, per-layer
  begin/finish over the channel, copy_cached_blobs for the prompt path, helper service-time counters.
- generate.cpp: SEABRAID_STRATA_SHM wiring, keep helper-held experts in the RAM copy unless SEABRAID_STRATA_EXCLUDE_HELPER_RAM=1,
  SEABRAID_STRATA_PTRACER diagnostic, per-request helper timing line.
- expert_source.cpp: route tail-skip stays on beside helper tiers (skips only experts no helper holds).
- CMake: SEABRAID_STRATA_SOURCE_DIR builds the helper from an external checkout.

The channel header this series used to create here (include/strata/seabraid/channel.hpp, extended by
0005/0007/0013/0014/0016, with expert_spec.hpp from 0007) is Seabraid's: adapters/strata/wire is its one owner.
This patch puts that directory on the include path (SEABRAID_WIRE_INCLUDE, derived from SEABRAID_STRATA_SOURCE_DIR)
instead of carrying a copy, so the adapter, the helper and this engine compile one definition of the bytes.
